            </rdf:Seq>
         </dc:creator>
         <dc:description>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Chinese-American law professor at Yale University, Amy Chua, smiles at the World Knowledge Forum in Seoul on October 13, 2011. Chua, as known as "Tiger Mom" after she sparked international controversy this year with her book "Battle Hymn of the Tiger Mother", urged strict Asian parents to relax and give their children more freedom but also to avoid the "romanticised" Western focus on creativity over hard work.   AFP PHOTO / LEE Seung-Hwan (Photo credit should read LEE Seung-Hwan/AFP via Getty Images)</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:description>
         <dc:rights>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">2011 AFP</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:rights>
